#, ai
msgid "<0>Play</0> walks the chapter stage by stage with AI-generated narration."
msgstr "<0>Main</0> menelusuri babak demi babak dalam bab ini dengan narasi yang dijana oleh AI."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#, ai
msgid "<0>Play</0> walks the chapter stage by stage. The captions keep time over a quiet wind."
msgstr "<0>Main</0> menelusuri babak demi babak dalam bab ini. Sarikata bergerak seiring masa berlatarkan bunyi angin yang tenang."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#, ai
msgid "<0>Ask</0> uses the chapter’s context to research in Turath and answer with source citations."
msgstr "<0>Tanya</0> menggunakan konteks bab ini untuk membuat rujukan dalam Turath dan menjawab berserta sumber rujukan."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This excerpt does not give an exact departure date."
msgstr "Petikan ini tidak menyatakan tarikh pelepasan yang tepat."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The excerpt describes preparations, not a nightly delivery to the cave."
msgstr "Petikan ini menggambarkan persiapan, bukannya penghantaran pada waktu malam ke gua tersebut."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The excerpt does not describe erasing footprints."
msgstr "Petikan ini tidak menggambarkan tindakan memadam kesan tapak kaki."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The account does not describe the cave’s dimensions or layout."
msgstr "Kisah ini tidak menggambarkan ukuran dimensi atau susun atur gua tersebut."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This excerpt is not the full verse and does not itself name Abu Bakr or Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Petikan ini bukanlah ayat yang lengkap dan tidak menyebut nama Abu Bakar atau Bukit Thawr secara khusus."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This is Ibn Kathir’s commentary, not the Quranic wording itself."
msgstr "Ini adalah tafsir Ibn Kathir, bukannya lafaz Al-Quran itu sendiri."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "It does not give an exact location for the stay among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf."
msgstr "Ia tidak memberikan lokasi yang tepat bagi tempoh tinggal dalam kalangan Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The passage does not name the place; identifying it as Quba rests on other reports."
msgstr "Petikan ini tidak menyebut nama tempat tersebut; pengenalpastiannya sebagai Quba bersandarkan kepada riwayat-riwayat lain."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The night of departure"
msgstr "Malam bertolak"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The leaders of Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah, the house where they settled their affairs, to decide what to do about the Prophet ﷺ now that they feared him."
msgstr "Para pemimpin Quraisy berkumpul di Dar al-Nadwah, rumah tempat mereka menyelesaikan urusan mereka, untuk memutuskan apa yang perlu dilakukan terhadap Nabi ﷺ setelah mereka merasa bimbang terhadap baginda."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "That night they gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak, and assured him that no harm from them would reach him."
msgstr "Pada malam itu mereka berkumpul di pintu rumah baginda, menunggu baginda tidur. Baginda menyuruh ‘Ali berbaring di tempat tidur baginda, berselimutkan jubah hijau baginda, dan meyakinkannya bahawa tiada bahaya daripada mereka yang akan menimpanya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "‘Ali stayed behind for another reason too. People in Makkah left their valuables with the Prophet ﷺ for safekeeping, because they knew his honesty. ‘Ali was to return every one of them."
msgstr "‘Ali tinggal di belakang atas satu sebab lain juga. Penduduk Makkah sering meninggalkan barang berharga mereka dengan Nabi ﷺ untuk disimpan dengan selamat, kerana mereka mengetahui kejujuran baginda. ‘Ali ditugaskan untuk mengembalikan setiap satu daripadanya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The tent of Umm Ma‘bad"
msgstr "Khemah Umm Ma‘bad"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Further on they stopped at the tent of Umm Ma‘bad of Khuza‘ah and asked for hospitality. She had no food to offer, she said, and no ewe but one that gave no milk."
msgstr "Seterusnya mereka singgah di khemah Umm Ma‘bad daripada suku Khuza‘ah dan meminta layanan sebagai tetamu. Dia berkata bahawa dia tidak mempunyai makanan untuk dihidangkan, dan tiada kambing melainkan seekor yang tidak mengeluarkan susu."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ called for the ewe, passed his hand over its udder and called on Allah. He milked it into a large vessel until it frothed, and said: drink, Umm Ma‘bad. Ibn Kathir notes that her story is well known and comes through routes that strengthen one another."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ meminta kambing itu dibawa, menyapu tangannya pada kantung susunya dan berdoa kepada Allah. Baginda memerah susunya ke dalam bekas yang besar sehingga berbuih, lalu bersabda: minumlah, wahai Umm Ma‘bad. Ibn Kathir menyatakan bahawa kisahnya amat terkenal dan diriwayatkan melalui jalur-jalur yang saling menguatkan antara satu sama lain."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq reports that Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah to consult about the Prophet ﷺ once they feared him."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq meriwayatkan bahawa Quraisy berkumpul di Dar al-Nadwah untuk bermesyuarat tentang Nabi ﷺ setelah mereka merasa bimbang terhadap baginda."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The excerpt covers the meeting, not what was said in it."
msgstr "Petikan ini merangkumi mesyuarat tersebut, bukannya apa yang diperkatakan di dalamnya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "They gathered at his door at night; he told ‘Ali to sleep in his bed under his green cloak and assured him of safety."
msgstr "Mereka berkumpul di pintu rumah baginda pada waktu malam; baginda menyuruh ‘Ali tidur di tempat tidur baginda di bawah jubah hijau baginda dan menjamin keselamatannya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Kathir notes that al-Waqidi also relates this, combining several narrators’ accounts."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir menyatakan bahawa al-Waqidi juga meriwayatkan perkara ini, dengan menggabungkan kisah daripada beberapa orang perawi."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq introduces this with “as it has reached me”."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq memulakan kisah ini dengan ungkapan \"sebagaimana yang telah sampai kepadaku\"."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "They stopped at Umm Ma‘bad’s tent; she had only a ewe without milk, which then gave milk in abundance."
msgstr "Mereka singgah di khemah Umm Ma‘bad; dia hanya mempunyai seekor kambing yang tidak menyusu, yang kemudiannya mengeluarkan susu dengan melimpah-limpah."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Kathir calls the story well known, through routes that support one another. It does not fix where the tent stood."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir menyifatkan kisah ini sebagai terkenal, melalui jalur-jalur yang saling menyokong antara satu sama lain. Ia tidak menetapkan di mana khemah itu berdiri."

#: src/content/details.js
#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Al-Rahiq al-Makhtum"
msgstr "Al-Rahiq al-Makhtum"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The noon visit"
msgstr "Ziarah waktu tengah hari"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "At the height of noon, an hour at which he never used to come, the Prophet ﷺ arrived at Abu Bakr’s house with his face covered. He said he had been given permission to leave. Abu Bakr asked to go with him, and he said yes."
msgstr "Pada kemuncak waktu tengah hari, satu waktu yang baginda tidak pernah biasa datang, Nabi ﷺ tiba di rumah Abu Bakar dengan wajah baginda yang tertutup. Baginda memberitahu bahawa baginda telah diberikan izin untuk keluar. Abu Bakar meminta untuk pergi bersama baginda, dan baginda bersetuju."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "This is ‘Aishah’s account as quoted in a modern sirah. The position of the house is illustrative."
msgstr "Ini adalah riwayat 'Aisyah seperti yang dipetik dalam sirah moden. Kedudukan rumah tersebut adalah sebagai ilustrasi sahaja."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Stones in the niche"
msgstr "Batu-batu di dalam lubang dinding"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money with him, five or six thousand dirhams. Asma recounts that her blind grandfather feared the family had been left with nothing. She put stones where the money used to be kept, covered them with a cloth, and guided his hand to them so that he would be at ease."
msgstr "Abu Bakar membawa semua wang bersamanya, sebanyak lima atau enam ribu dirham. Asma menceritakan bahawa datuknya yang buta bimbang keluarga mereka ditinggalkan tanpa apa-apa. Beliau meletakkan batu-batu di tempat wang biasa disimpan, menutupnya dengan sehelai kain, dan memandu tangan datuknya ke arah batu-batu itu agar hatinya tenang."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Reported by Ibn Ishaq from Asma through her grandson. The position of the house is illustrative."
msgstr "Diriwayatkan oleh Ibn Ishaq daripada Asma melalui cucunya. Kedudukan rumah tersebut adalah sebagai ilustrasi sahaja."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Why south?"
msgstr "Mengapa ke selatan?"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Madinah lies to the north, and that is where a search would begin. They left in the opposite direction, on the road towards Yemen, for about five miles to Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah terletak di sebelah utara, dan di situlah pencarian akan bermula. Mereka bertolak ke arah yang bertentangan, di jalan menuju ke Yaman, sejauh kira-kira lima batu ke Bukit Thawr."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "This is a modern author’s reading of the route, not wording from an early report."
msgstr "Ini adalah tafsiran laluan oleh pengarang moden, bukan lafaz daripada riwayat awal."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "She of the two belts"
msgstr "Wanita yang mempunyai dua tali pinggang"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "When the three nights had passed, Asma brought their provisions but had forgotten a strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and used it. For that she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn, she of the two belts."
msgstr "Apabila tiga malam telah berlalu, Asma membawa bekalan mereka tetapi terlupa tali untuk menggantung beg tersebut. Beliau membuka tali pinggangnya dan menggunakannya. Disebabkan itu, beliau digelar Dhat al-Nitaqayn, wanita yang mempunyai dua tali pinggang."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s report. ‘Aishah’s account in al-Bukhari places the belt at the packing of the provisions instead."
msgstr "Riwayat Ibn Ishaq. Riwayat 'Aisyah dalam al-Bukhari pula menyatakan tali pinggang itu digunakan semasa penyediaan bekalan."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The spider’s web"
msgstr "Sarang labah-labah"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "One report says the pursuers climbed the mountain, passed the cave, and saw a spider’s web across its opening. No one could have gone in, they reasoned, and they moved on. Ibn Kathir calls its chain good, the best of what is reported on this. The scene does not draw the web."
msgstr "Satu riwayat menyebut bahawa para pengejar mendaki gunung tersebut, melepasi gua itu, dan melihat sarang labah-labah di pintu masuknya. Mereka berfikir tiada sesiapa yang boleh masuk ke dalam, lalu mereka berlalu pergi. Ibn Kathir menyebut sanadnya adalah baik, yang terbaik antara apa yang diriwayatkan tentang perkara ini. Visual ini tidak melukis sarang labah-labah tersebut."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "A single report. The nesting doves of popular retellings are not part of it."
msgstr "Satu riwayat tunggal. Burung merpati yang bersarang dalam penceritaan popular bukan sebahagian daripadanya."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The stations of the road"
msgstr "Persinggahan di sepanjang jalan"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq names the way the guide took: below Makkah, along the coast, across the road below ‘Usfan, below Amaj, past Qudayd, then al-Kharrar, Thaniyyat al-Marah, Liqf and on. Many of these names are hard to place today, so the line drawn here stays approximate."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menamakan jalan yang dilalui oleh penunjuk jalan: di bawah Makkah, menyusuri pantai, merentasi jalan di bawah 'Usfan, di bawah Amaj, melepasi Qudayd, kemudian al-Kharrar, Thaniyyat al-Marah, Liqf dan seterusnya. Kebanyakan nama ini sukar untuk dikesan kedudukannya hari ini, jadi garisan yang dilukis di sini kekal sebagai anggaran sahaja."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "A list of names, without distances or days."
msgstr "Senarai nama, tanpa jarak atau hari."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "White garments"
msgstr "Pakaian putih"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "On the way they met al-Zubayr with a group of Muslim merchants returning from Syria. He gave the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr white garments to wear."
msgstr "Dalam perjalanan, mereka bertemu al-Zubayr bersama sekumpulan pedagang Muslim yang sedang pulang dari Syam. Beliau memberikan Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakar pakaian putih untuk dipakai."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "From al-Bukhari, as quoted by Ibn Kathir. The account does not say where on the road they met."
msgstr "Daripada al-Bukhari, seperti yang dipetik oleh Ibn Kathir. Riwayat tersebut tidak menyatakan di bahagian jalan mana mereka bertemu."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The first Friday"
msgstr "Solat Jumaat yang pertama"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "After leaving Quba, the time for Friday prayer came while he was among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf. He led it there, in the mosque in the bed of the valley, with about a hundred men."
msgstr "Selepas meninggalkan Quba, waktu solat Jumaat masuk ketika baginda berada di kalangan Bani Salim ibn 'Awf. Baginda mengimami solat di sana, di masjid yang terletak di dasar lembah, bersama kira-kira seratus orang lelaki."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Quoted from a modern sirah, which cites Ibn Hisham. The position is illustrative."
msgstr "Dipetik daripada sirah moden, yang merujuk kepada Ibn Hisham. Kedudukannya adalah sebagai ilustrasi sahaja."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Let her go"
msgstr "Biarkan dia pergi"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Clan after clan took hold of his camel’s rope and invited him to stay with them. Each time he answered: let her go, for she is under command. She walked on until she knelt in the quarter of Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Kabilah demi kabilah memegang tali unta baginda dan menjemput baginda untuk tinggal bersama mereka. Setiap kali itu baginda menjawab: biarkan dia pergi, kerana dia di bawah perintah. Unta itu terus berjalan sehingga ia berlutut di kawasan Bani Malik ibn al-Najjar."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s report. Her path through the town is not known."
msgstr "Riwayat Ibn Ishaq. Laluan unta itu melalui bandar tersebut tidak diketahui."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The house of Abu Ayyub"
msgstr "Rumah Abu Ayyub"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "He stayed in the house of Abu Ayyub until his mosque and his rooms were built, and he worked on the building himself alongside the Muhajirun and the Ansar."
msgstr "Baginda tinggal di rumah Abu Ayyub sehingga masjid dan bilik-bilik baginda siap dibina, dan baginda sendiri turut bekerja membina bangunan tersebut bersama-sama golongan Muhajirin dan Ansar."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The house is placed beside the mosque site for illustration."
msgstr "Rumah tersebut diletakkan di sebelah tapak masjid sebagai ilustrasi sahaja."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Brothers"
msgstr "Persaudaraan"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "He paired those who had migrated with those who received them, as brothers, so that each newcomer had someone to lean on."
msgstr "Baginda mempersaudarakan mereka yang berhijrah dengan mereka yang menyambut mereka, supaya setiap pendatang baharu mempunyai seseorang untuk bergantung."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "This is Ibn Kathir’s chapter heading. The individual pairings are listed in the pages that follow it."
msgstr "Ini adalah tajuk bab daripada Ibn Kathir. Pasangan individu disenaraikan dalam halaman-halaman yang menyusulinya."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The full moon has risen"
msgstr "Telah terbit bulan purnama atas kita"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "A well-known report says the women and children sang “The full moon has risen upon us, from the passes of al-Wada‘” when he arrived. Al-Bayhaqi relates it from Ibn ‘Aishah, a later narrator, not from someone who was there."
msgstr "Satu riwayat yang terkenal menyebut bahawa kaum wanita dan kanak-kanak mendendangkan \"Tala'al badru 'alayna, min thaniyyatil-wada'\" semasa baginda tiba. Al-Bayhaqi meriwayatkannya daripada Ibn 'Aisyah, seorang perawi terkemudian, bukan daripada seseorang yang berada di tempat kejadian."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The chain stops short of an eyewitness, and some place the song at a later return to Madinah, not at this arrival."
msgstr "Rantaian sanadnya terputus sebelum sampai kepada saksi mata, dan sesetengah pihak berpendapat lagu itu didendangkan semasa kepulangan baginda ke Madinah yang terkemudian, bukan semasa ketibaan ini."

